// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 21-standard-library-semantics
// facility: rule.stdlib.str `[Str-Literal-View]` (D-0134): only a literal is typed by its position; conf.view-of-str-binding-rejected
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.type-mismatch (static)
//
// A `str` binding has type `str`; it becomes a view only by
// `StringView::of(t)`. Implicit conversions do not exist (D-0006).

import std;

fn main()
{
    str t = "abc";
    StringView v = t;
}
